{
  "biological_interpretation": "MEF2 paralog identity matters: MEF2C loss preferentially remodels cortical IT excitatory neurons, whereas MEF2A loss resolves to a narrower thalamic marker set.",
  "caveats": [
    "The cortical Mef2c module is not explained by a strong in-dataset phenocopy; Celf2/Cic relationships remain weak thalamic follow-ups, not causal assignments.",
    "Mef2a and Mef2c have different target-engagement profiles, which contributes to the paralog contrast."
  ],
  "cell_types": [
    "005 L4-5 IT CTX Glut",
    "007 L2-3 IT CTX Glut",
    "151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut"
  ],
  "exact_observed_result": "Mef2c perturbation drove a cortical IT synaptic/membrane program in 005 L4-5 and 007 L2-3 IT CTX Glut, while Mef2a\u2019s FDR-supported downstream response was restricted to 151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut with Gpr4, Ogt, Prkcg, and Sez6. No assayed perturbation was a strong Mef2c-like or anti-Mef2c neighbor in the two high-signal cortical classes.",
  "preliminary_scores": {
